<title>UK: LME copper firmer in AM, but seen vulnerable.</title>
<headline>LME copper firmer in AM, but seen vulnerable.</headline>
<text>
<p>COPPER - Up some $25 from Wednesday kerb close at $2,262/2,266. Seen consolidating after sharp falls but vulnerable to downside, towards $2,200. LME stocks unsupportive, up 2,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>ALUMINIUM - Touch firmer at $1,573/1,575.</p>
<p>OTHERS - Also generally firmer.</p>
</text>
